1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:03,414
Fingers cold, white and numb after time in the cold?

2
00:00:03,414 --> 00:00:05,178
Know frostnip from frostbite.

3
00:00:05,880 --> 00:00:09,327
Frostnip: skin turns red or pale, cold and tingly.

4
00:00:09,327 --> 00:00:11,533
It recovers fully once rewarmed.

5
00:00:12,230 --> 00:00:13,882
Frostbite: tissue freezes.

6
00:00:13,882 --> 00:00:18,075
Skin may look white, grey or blue, feel hard or waxy, and go numb.

7
00:00:18,780 --> 00:00:20,138
1 — Get somewhere warm.

8
00:00:20,138 --> 00:00:22,321
Remove wet clothes, gloves and rings.

9
00:00:24,280 --> 00:00:32,707
2 — Rewarm in warm, not hot water (about 37 to 39 degrees Celsius) for 15 to 30 minutes, or use body heat.

10
00:00:33,410 --> 00:00:38,359
Don't rub it, and no direct heat — fires, heaters or hot pads can burn numb skin.

11
00:00:39,410 --> 00:00:41,294
Frostbite needs medical care.

12
00:00:41,294 --> 00:00:45,127
Get help if skin stays numb, hard, blistered or turns dark.
